 types \"Bob\", selects \"Bob Jones\", then repeats to select \"Carol Lee\"\n  1364→- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Carol Lee\" after the final selection. Each selection correctly replaces the previous one.\n  1365→\n  1366→#### Test: Labels selector can be used multiple times in sequence\n  1367→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with no labels selected\n  1368→- **Action**: User selects \"Bug\" label, then opens the selector again and adds \"Feature\", then opens again and removes \"Bug\" and adds \"Improvement\"\n  1369→- **Expected**: Labels field shows \"Feature\" and \"Improvement\" as colored badges.\n  1370→\n  1371→#### Test: Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n  1372→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with Status \"Backlog\"\n  1373→- **Action**: User changes status to \"Todo\", then changes it to \"In Progress\", then back to \"Backlog\"\n  1374→- **Expected**: Status shows \"Backlog\" after the final change. Each intermediate state was correctly displayed.\n  1375→\n  1376→### CreateIssueActions\n  1377→\n  1378→#### Test: Create Issue button is visible and styled\n  1379→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1380→- **Expected**: A \"Create Issue\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal with primary styling (accent color background).\n  1381→\n  1382→#### Test: Cancel button is visible\n  1383→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1384→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal alongside the \"Create Issue\" button.\n  1385→\n  1386→#### Test: Cancel button closes the modal\n  1387→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1388→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1389→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No issue is created. The user returns to the previous page view.\n  1390→\n  1391→#### Test: Cancel button discards form data\n  1392→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has entered title \"Draft issue\" and selected priority \"High\".\n  1393→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\", then opens the create issue modal again\n  1394→- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields reset to defaults (empty title, Backlog status, No Priority). The previously entered data is not retained.\n  1395→\n  1396→#### Test: Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n  1397→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has filled in: Title \"Implement OAuth\", Description \"Add OAuth support\", Status \"Todo\", Priority \"High\", Assignee \"Alice Smith\", Labels \"Feature\", Project \"API Redesign\", Cycle \"Sprint 10\", Due date \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n  1398→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1399→- **Expected**: The issue is created with all specified field values. A brief confirmation showing the new issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-43\") is displayed. The modal closes and the user is navigated to the issues list.\n  1400→\n  1401→#### Test: Create Issue with only required fields\n  1402→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected\n  1403→- **Action**: User enters title \"Quick bug fix\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1404→- **Expected**: The issue is created with title \"Quick bug fix\", status \"Backlog\", priority \"No Priority\", and no assignee/labels/project/cycle/due date. The new issue identifier is briefly shown. The modal closes.\n  1405→\n  1406→#### Test: Created issue appears in the team issues list\n  1407→- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for \"Engineering\". The page shows existing issues.\n  1408→- **Action**: User clicks \"New Issue\", enters title \"New feature request\", sets status to \"Todo\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1409→- **Expected**: After modal closes, the Team Issues list updates to include \"New feature request\" under the \"Todo\" status group with the correct issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-44\").\n  1410→\n  1411→#### Test: Created issue with parent appears as sub-issue\n  1412→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issue \"ENG-1: Setup project\" exists.\n  1413→- **Action**: User enters title \"Write unit tests\", selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\" as parent issue, and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1414→- **Expected**: The issue is created. When navigating to \"ENG-1: Setup project\" detail page, \"Write unit tests\" appears in the sub-issues section.\n  1415→\n  1416→#### Test: Created issue generates activity history entry\n  1417→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1418→- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Track history\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1419→- **Expected**: When viewing the new issue's detail page, the Activity tab shows an initial \"created this issue\" entry with the current user's name and timestamp."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016e1ckREppSeN1K5Dw6jKKC","session_id":"fb1ffc50-dd2f-4394-84c9-ce4b197eaf03","uuid":"6d1a649f-9c88-49b2-b5e9-b664bb6e00f5"}
