[2026-03-14T19:30:39.892Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016e1ckREppSeN1K5Dw6jKKC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary report:\n\n## Comprehensive Linear Clone App Exploration Report\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY NAME AND STRUCTURE\n\n**App Directory:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone`\n\n**Structure:**\n```\nLinearClone/\n├── AppSpec.md                    # Full application specification\n├── docs/\n│   └── tests.md                  # Comprehensive test specifications (2685 lines)\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/               # React components with CSS\n│   ├── pages/                    # Page components\n│   ├── slices/                   # Redux slices for state management\n│   └── store.ts                  # Redux store configuration\n└── netlify/\n    └── functions/                # Serverless backend functions\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. APPSPEC.MD - FULL CONTENT SUMMARY\n\nThe complete AppSpec is available at `/repo/apps/LinearClone/AppSpec.md`. Key sections include:\n\n**Core Features:**\n- Workspace, Team, Project, Issue, Cycle, Label, Member management\n- Email-based authentication (no OAuth)\n- Keyboard shortcuts (C for create issue, G+I for My Issues, G+N for Inbox)\n\n**Pages:**\n- Login (`/login`) & Sign Up (`/signup`)\n- My Issues (`/my-issues`) - filtered by current user\n- Inbox (`/inbox`) - notifications\n- Team Issues (`/team/:teamId/issues`) - with grouping, sorting, filtering, bulk actions\n- Issue Detail (`/issue/:issueId`) - full editing and activity/comments\n- Active Cycle (`/team/:teamId/cycles`)\n- Projects (`/projects`) & Project Detail (`/project/:projectId`)\n- Members (`/settings/members`)\n- Teams Management (`/settings/teams`)\n- Labels (`/settings/labels`)\n- Settings (`/settings`)\n\n**Issue Statuses & Priorities:**\n- Statuses: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled\n- Priorities: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority\n\n**Create Issue Modal:**\n- Required: Team, Title\n- Optional: Description, Status, Priority, Assignee, Labels, Project, Cycle, Due date, Parent issue\n\n**Visual Design:**\n- Dark mode by default\n- Colors: bg `#0f1117`, surface `#1a1d24`, borders `#2a2d35`, accent `#5e6ad2`\n- System font stack (Inter preferred)\n\n---\n\n### 3. DOCS/TESTS.MD - CreateIssue SECTION\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (lines 1224-1443)\n\n**Key Test Sections:**\n\n**CreateIssueForm Tests (lines 1228-1375):**\n- Modal renders all form fields\n- Modal opens from \"New Issue\" button and keyboard shortcut C\n- Team selector defaults to current team context\n- Title field is required\n- Description supports markdown\n- Status defaults to \"Backlog\"\n- Priority defaults to \"No Priority\"\n- Assignee selector is searchable\n- Labels multi-select allows multiple selections\n- Project selector is searchable\n- Cycle dropdown shows team's cycles and updates when team changes\n- Due date picker with clear button\n- Parent issue selector for sub-issues\n- All selectors can be used multiple times\n\n**CreateIssueActions Tests (lines 1376-1424):**\n- \"Create Issue\" button submits with all fields\n- \"Cancel\" button closes and resets form\n- Issue created with only required fields (title + team)\n- Issue created with full set of fields including assignee, labels, project, cycle, due date\n- Issue identifier briefly displayed after creation\n- Modal closes and user navigated to issues list\n- Sub-issues appear in parent's detail page\n- Activity history entry created for new issue\n- Created issue appears in team issues list\n\n---\n\n### 4. APPSTYLE.MD\n\n**No AppStyle.md file exists.** The style guidance is embedded in the AppSpec.md under \"Visual Design\" section (lines 280-288).\n\n---\n\n### 5. REDUX SLICES\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/`\n\n**Available Slices:**\n\n1. **authSlice.ts** - Authentication state\n   - Actions: `login()`, `signup()`, `fetchCurrentUser()`\n   - State: user, token, loading, error\n   - Stores session token in localStorage\n\n2. **uiSlice.ts** - UI state\n   - State: `sidebarCollapsed`, `createIssueModalOpen`\n   - Actions: `toggleSidebar()`, `openCreateIssueModal()`, `closeCreateIssueModal()`\n\n3. **issuesSlice.ts** - My Issues\n   - State: `myIssues[]`, loading, error\n   - Actions: `fetchMyIssues()`, `updateIssueStatus()`\n   - Issue interface includes: id, title, description, status, priority, identifier, number, dueDate, createdAt, updatedAt, teamId, teamName, assigneeId, assigneeName, assigneeEmail, projectId, projectName, cycleId, parentId, labels[]\n\n4. **teamsSlice.ts** - Teams\n   - State: `items[]`, loading, error\n   - Action: `fetchTeams()`\n\n5. **labelsSlice.ts** - Labels\n   - State: `items[]`, loading, error\n   - Action: `fetchLabels()`\n\n6. **teamIssuesSlice.ts** - Team Issues\n   - State: `items[]`, `members[]`, `projects[]`, `cycles[]`, `selectedIds[]`, `groupBy`, `sortBy`\n   - Actions: `fetchTeamIssues()`, `bulkUpdateIssues()`\n   - Reducers: `toggleIssueSelection()`, `selectGroupIssues()`, `clearSelection()`, `setGroupBy()`, `setSortBy()`\n\n7. **notificationsSlice.ts** - Notifications\n   - State: `unreadCount`, `items[]`, loading\n   - Actions: `fetchUnreadCount()`, `fetchNotifications()`, `markNotificationRead()`, `archiveNotification()`\n\n8. **workspaceSlice.ts** - Workspace\n   - State: `workspace`, loading, error\n   - Action: `fetchWorkspace()`\n\n---\n\n### 6. EXISTING COMPONENTS FOR REFERENCE\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/`\n\n**Components:**\n1. **IssueRow.tsx** - Displays individual issue with status/priority icons, title, labels, project, due date, assignee avatar\n   - Includes helper functions: `StatusIcon()`, `PriorityIcon()`, `getInitials()`, `formatDueDate()`\n   - Exports: `STATUS_CONFIG`, `PRIORITY_CONFIG`, `STATUS_ORDER`\n   - Props: issue, showCheckbox, checked, onCheckChange\n\n2. **BulkActions.tsx** - Bulk selection toolbar with dropdowns for status, priority, assignee, label\n   - Uses inline state for `openDropdown`\n   - Dispatches: `bulkUpdateIssues()`, `clearSelection()`\n\n3. **LoginForm.tsx** - Email/password form with validation\n   - Uses local state for form fields and validation errors\n   - Dispatches: `login()`, `clearError()`\n\n4. **TeamIssuesList.tsx** - Lists issues in a grid format\n5. **MyIssuesList.tsx** - My issues variant\n6. **TeamFilters.tsx** - Multi-select filter dropdowns\n7. **GroupBySort.tsx** - Group and sort controls\n8. **Sidebar.tsx** - Navigation sidebar\n9. **NotificationList.tsx** & **NotificationRow.tsx** - Notifications\n10. **KeyboardShortcuts.tsx** - Keyboard shortcut handler\n\n---\n\n### 7. DATABASE SCHEMA\n\n**No explicit schema file exists at `/repo/scripts/schema.ts`.** \n\n**Database references inferred from API functions at `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/`:**\n\n**Tables referenced:**\n- `members` - id, name, email\n- `sessions` - token, expires_at, member_id\n- `teams` - id, name, identifier, description\n- `issues` - id, title, description, status, priority, number, due_date, created_at, updated_at, team_id, assignee_id, project_id, cycle_id, parent_id\n- `issue_labels` - issue_id, label_id\n- `labels` - id, name, color\n- `projects` - id, name\n- `cycles` - id, name, start_date, end_date, team_id\n- `team_members` - team_id, member_id\n\n**Neon database backend** uses `neon()` from `@neondatabase/serverless`\n\n---\n\n### 8. EXISTING MODAL PATTERNS\n\n**Modal Control:**\n- No dedicated modal component library (no shadcn/ui modals currently used)\n- Modal state managed via Redux `uiSlice.ts`:\n  - `createIssueModalOpen` boolean state\n  - Actions: `openCreateIssueModal()`, `closeCreateIssueModal()`\n\n**Modal opening pattern in pages:**\n```typescript\nfunction handleNewIssue() {\n  dispatch(openCreateIssueModal());\n}\n```\n\n**Example from TeamIssues.tsx (line 76-78):**\n- New Issue button dispatches `openCreateIssueModal()`\n- No existing modal component found in rendered JSX yet\n\n---\n\n### 9. BACKEND FUNCTIONS FOR ISSUES\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/`\n\n**Existing API Functions:**\n\n1. **team-issues.ts** - GET `/api/team-issues?teamId=`\n   - Fetches all team issues with joins to teams, projects, members, cycles, labels\n   - Returns: issues[], members[], projects[], cycles[]\n   - Auth: Bearer token required\n\n2. **my-issues.ts** - GET `/api/my-issues`\n   - Fetches issues assigned to current user\n   - Returns: issues[]\n   - Auth: Bearer token required\n\n3. **update-issue-status.ts** - PUT `/api/update-issue-status`\n   - Updates single issue status\n   - Body: { issueId, status }\n   - Returns: { issue: { id, status } }\n   - Auth: Bearer token required\n\n4. **bulk-update-issues.ts** - PUT `/api/bulk-update-issues`\n   - Updates multiple issues with status, priority, assigneeId, or labelId\n   - Body: { issueIds[], status?, priority?, assigneeId?, labelId? }\n   - Auth: Bearer token required\n\n5. **labels.ts** - GET `/api/labels`\n   - Returns all labels\n   - Returns: { labels[] }\n\n6. **login.ts** - POST `/api/login`\n   - Email/password authentication\n   - Returns: { user: { id, name, email }, token }\n\n7. **signup.ts** - POST `/api/signup`\n   - Creates new user and workspace\n   - Returns: { user: { id, name, email }, token }\n\n8. **teams.ts** - GET `/api/teams`\n   - Fetches all teams for workspace\n\n9. **notifications.ts** - GET `/api/notifications`\n10. **notifications-count.ts** - GET `/api/notifications-count`\n11. **workspace.ts** - GET `/api/workspace`\n12. **me.ts** - GET `/api/me` (current user)\n\n**CRITICAL: No CREATE ISSUE API endpoint exists yet** - this will need to be implemented\n\n---\n\n### 10. STORE CONFIGURATION\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\n\n```typescript\nconst store = configureStore({\n  reducer: {\n    auth: authReducer,\n    ui: 