[2026-03-14T19:30:51.828Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTzYSWn7hRx6zaAzqNk8fX","type":"tool_result","content":"  1224→## Create Issue Modal\n  1225→\n  1226→**Components**: CreateIssueForm, CreateIssueActions\n  1227→\n  1228→### CreateIssueForm\n  1229→\n  1230→#### Test: Create issue modal renders with all form fields\n  1231→- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for team \"Engineering\"\n  1232→- **Expected**: Modal displays: Team selector dropdown, Title text input, Description text area, Status dropdown, Priority dropdown, Assignee searchable selector, Labels multi-select, Project searchable selector, Cycle dropdown, Due date picker, and Parent issue searchable selector. All fields are visible and properly labeled.\n  1233→\n  1234→#### Test: Modal opens from New Issue button on team issues page\n  1235→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/:teamId/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n  1236→- **Action**: User clicks the \"New Issue\" button\n  1237→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens as an overlay. The Team selector is pre-selected to \"Engineering\". The Title input is focused.\n  1238→\n  1239→#### Test: Modal opens from keyboard shortcut C\n  1240→- **Initial state**: User is on `/my-issues`, no input fields are focused\n  1241→- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n  1242→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens as an overlay.\n  1243→\n  1244→#### Test: Team selector defaults to current team context\n  1245→- **Initial state**: User opens create issue modal from team \"Design\" issues page\n  1246→- **Expected**: The Team selector dropdown shows \"Design\" as the selected value.\n  1247→\n  1248→#### Test: Team selector allows changing team\n  1249→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" pre-selected. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n  1250→- **Action**: User clicks the Team selector dropdown and selects \"Design\"\n  1251→- **Expected**: Team selector now shows \"Design\". The Cycle dropdown updates to show \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" team's cycles.\n  1252→\n  1253→#### Test: Title field is required\n  1254→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1255→- **Action**: User leaves the Title field empty and attempts to submit\n  1256→- **Expected**: A validation error appears indicating that title is required. The issue is not created.\n  1257→\n  1258→#### Test: Title field accepts text input\n  1259→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1260→- **Action**: User types \"Implement user authentication\" in the Title field\n  1261→- **Expected**: The Title field displays \"Implement user authentication\".\n  1262→\n  1263→#### Test: Description field supports markdown text entry\n  1264→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1265→- **Action**: User types \"## Overview\\nThis issue covers the auth flow\" in the Description text area\n  1266→- **Expected**: The Description field accepts and displays the markdown text.\n  1267→\n  1268→#### Test: Status dropdown defaults to Backlog\n  1269→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1270→- **Expected**: The Status dropdown shows \"Backlog\" with a dotted circle icon in gray as the default selected value.\n  1271→\n  1272→#### Test: Status dropdown shows all status options with icons\n  1273→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1274→- **Action**: User clicks the Status dropdown\n  1275→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red).\n  1276→\n  1277→#### Test: Status dropdown allows selecting a different status\n  1278→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Status shows \"Backlog\"\n  1279→- **Action**: User clicks Status dropdown and selects \"Todo\"\n  1280→- **Expected**: Status dropdown now shows \"Todo\" with circle icon in gray.\n  1281→\n  1282→#### Test: Priority dropdown defaults to No Priority\n  1283→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1284→- **Expected**: The Priority dropdown shows \"No Priority\" with dots-horizontal icon in gray as the default value.\n  1285→\n  1286→#### Test: Priority dropdown shows all priority options with icons\n  1287→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1288→- **Action**: User clicks the Priority dropdown\n  1289→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray).\n  1290→\n  1291→#### Test: Priority dropdown allows selecting a priority\n  1292→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Priority shows \"No Priority\"\n  1293→- **Action**: User clicks Priority dropdown and selects \"High\"\n  1294→- **Expected**: Priority dropdown now shows \"High\" with arrow-up icon in orange.\n  1295→\n  1296→#### Test: Assignee selector is searchable\n  1297→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\", \"Carol Lee\".\n  1298→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector and types \"Ali\"\n  1299→- **Expected**: The selector filters to show only \"Alice Smith\" with her avatar.\n  1300→\n  1301→#### Test: Assignee selector allows selecting a member\n  1302→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Assignee field is empty\n  1303→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector, types \"Bob\", and clicks \"Bob Jones\"\n  1304→- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Bob Jones\" with his avatar.\n  1305→\n  1306→#### Test: Labels multi-select allows selecting multiple labels\n  1307→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Labels \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\" exist.\n  1308→- **Action**: User clicks Labels selector, selects \"Bug\", then selects \"Feature\"\n  1309→- **Expected**: Both \"Bug\" and \"Feature\