*: User selects \"Bug\" label, then opens the selector again and adds \"Feature\", then opens again and removes \"Bug\" and adds \"Improvement\"\n  1369→- **Expected**: Labels field shows \"Feature\" and \"Improvement\" as colored badges.\n  1370→\n  1371→#### Test: Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n  1372→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with Status \"Backlog\"\n  1373→- **Action**: User changes status to \"Todo\", then changes it to \"In Progress\", then back to \"Backlog\"\n  1374→- **Expected**: Status shows \"Backlog\" after the final change. Each intermediate state was correctly displayed.\n  1375→\n  1376→### CreateIssueActions\n  1377→\n  1378→#### Test: Create Issue button is visible and styled\n  1379→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1380→- **Expected**: A \"Create Issue\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal with primary styling (accent color background).\n  1381→\n  1382→#### Test: Cancel button is visible\n  1383→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1384→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal alongside the \"Create Issue\" button.\n  1385→\n  1386→#### Test: Cancel button closes the modal\n  1387→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1388→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1389→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No issue is created. The user returns to the previous page view.\n  1390→\n  1391→#### Test: Cancel button discards form data\n  1392→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has entered title \"Draft issue\" and selected priority \"High\".\n  1393→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\", then opens the create issue modal again\n  1394→- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields reset to defaults (empty title, Backlog status, No Priority). The previously entered data is not retained.\n  1395→\n  1396→#### Test: Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n  1397→- **Initial state**: Create issu